Subject: Philosophical question about tourr
Message-ID: <1o8InbS5wmc.EhMkqLKMWEEJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggvis/c/1o8InbS5wmc/m/EhMkqLKMWEEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I have spent some time being impressed/hypnotized by the tourr demo.

Looking at the code, I see it uses reactive calls in conjunction with shiny.

The demo works well self-contained on my laptop.

Would it / could it work well as a web-deployed shiny app? Or would it / could it get bogged down (esp. with many points) in server/client communications, updating for each frame?

This is not a feature request or suggestion - you guys are busy enough. It's just me trying to sort out how all this stuff might be able to work together for the foreseeable future.

Thanks!

From ub756a7daa2c2aa6d at groups.google.com  Fri Feb 21 16:08:01 2014
From: ub756a7daa2c2aa6d at groups.google.com (Hadley Wickham)
Date: Fri, 21 Feb 2014 16:08:01 +0000
Subject: Re: Philosophical question about tourr
Message-ID: <1o8InbS5wmc.zdxZpqZ_TmQJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <1o8InbS5wmc.EhMkqLKMWEEJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
References: <1o8InbS5wmc.EhMkqLKMWEEJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggvis/c/1o8InbS5wmc/m/zdxZpqZ_TmQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It may get bogged down, but we still have a lot of optimisation to do.
ggvis is always going to be faster when used locally, but I think most
common that don't involve sending heaps of data around should be fine
remotely as well.

Hadley

