Hi,

Firstly, big congrats to the release of ggvis 0.1.

Secondly, I have a question regarding properties in axis. The same question was also mentioned before.
I used ggvis 0.1 and tried the code presented on the ggvis website (http://ggvis.rstudio.com/axes-legends.html#custom-styles)
ggvis(mtcars, props(x = ~wt, y = ~mpg)) +
  mark_symbol() +
  guide_axis("x", properties = list(
    axis = props(stroke = "red", strokeWidth = 5),
    grid = props(stroke = "blue"),
    ticks = props(stroke = "blue", strokeWidth = 2),
    labels = props(angle = 45, align = "left", fontSize = 20)
  ))
I am not sure how the properties work on the axis. I thought in the resulting picture, the x axis should be red and ticks on the x axis should be blue. However, it's not. Do I miss something here?

Another question, after I make a plot using ggvis, is there any function that allow me to get the javascript (html) code for the plot? It might be helpful for checking the result from R code along with javascript code for vega).

Thanks.

